; bfsodium SHA_256 : FIPS 180_4
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The round and the schedule step are each PASTED from
; their own verified files  so this file is the table  the two conveyors and
; the plumbing that joins them;
;
; IO  in:  len{2} LE  msg{len}
;     out: digest{32}       big endian  as the standard prints it
;
; The length prefix is how the program knows where the message ends; a bfsodium
; primitive never relies on end of input;
;
; SHA_256 is big endian on the wire and bfsodium is little endian inside
; (CONVENTIONS section 2)  so every word is reversed as it is loaded and again
; as the digest is written; that is the only place endianness is touched;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x01f  H{8}     u32 LE  the running hash
;   @0x020:0x03f  v{8}     u32 LE  a b c d e f g h  the working variables
;   @0x040:0x07f  w{16}    u32 LE  the schedule window
;   @0x080:0x083  Wt{4}    u32 LE  this round's schedule word; SPENT by the round
;   @0x084:0x087  Wc{4}    u32 LE  a copy of it  which the window keeps
;   @0x088        pre      u8      sixteen while the schedule is still message
;   @0x089        rnd      u8      rounds remaining
;   @0x08a        f16      u8      set when this round's word comes from the window
;   @0x08b        nf       u8      the complement of f16
;   @0x08c        tt       u8      a copy  so a count can be tested without being eaten
;   @0x08d        uu       u8      puts that copy back
;   @0x090:0x093  tmp{4}   u32 LE  hands a word back after it has been copied
;   @0x098:0x0ab  the adder frame; add32 footprint 0:19 at @0x098
;   @0x0b0:0x16c  sha256/round's frame; its footprint is 0:188 pasted at @0x0b0
;   @0x170:0x1f4  sha256/expand's frame; its footprint is 0:132 at @0x170
;   @0x200:0x2ff  K{64}    u32 LE  the round constants; the table is SHIFTED one
;                          word left per round  so K{t} is always at @0x200 and
;                          no index is ever computed
;   @0x300:0x33f  blk{64}  u8      the block  big endian on the wire
;
; TWO CONVEYORS AND NO INDEX; the schedule window holds sixteen words and every
; tap the recurrence wants sits at a fixed place in it: W{t minus 16} at w{0}
; W{t minus 15} at w{1}  W{t minus 7} at w{9} and W{t minus 2} at w{14}; the
; window rotates one word left per round and the word just used is written into
; w{15}  which is what puts the next round's taps in the same four cells again;
; The constants are the same trick: the table shifts one word left per round so
; the round always reads the head of it;
;
; The first sixteen rounds take their word straight from the window and the
; other forty eight compute one; that is the only conditional here  and it is
; driven by a counter rather than by comparing t against sixteen;

; ==== the sixty four round constants ====
; A table because the rounds are a loop; unrolling sixty four rounds to inline
; them is the size explosion the budget forbids; Each byte is the shorter of
; counting up from nought or down through the wrap  and each line is one
; constant  four bytes little endian;
; to the head of the table
R512
; ASSERT ptr=512
; K 0 is 0x428a2f98
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++>---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++>
